1
00:00:22,540 --> 00:00:24,370
Get indoors as quickly as you can!

2
00:00:24,370 --> 00:00:26,000
Th-Thank you!

3
00:00:28,590 --> 00:00:29,960
Wh-What in the world?

4
00:00:29,960 --> 00:00:31,710
What are these creatures?

5
00:00:32,130 --> 00:00:33,420
Galilea.

6
00:00:33,420 --> 00:00:36,140
Yeah. Looks like it's starting.

7
00:00:36,510 --> 00:00:39,510
This is a lot worse than 
our worst case scenario.

8
00:00:39,510 --> 00:00:40,510
Nah.

9
00:00:40,760 --> 00:00:42,560
It's actually precisely as expected...

10
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:47,980
as far as Prince Lloyd is concerned.

11
00:00:57,990 --> 00:01:02,870
I Was Reincarnated as the 7th Prince

12
00:00:57,990 --> 00:01:02,870
so I Can Take My Time
Perfecting My Magical Ability 2nd Season

13
00:02:19,030 --> 00:02:21,490
Days Ago

14
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:21,060
Saria...

15
00:02:21,690 --> 00:02:25,230
Can I be a part of your recital?

16
00:02:25,230 --> 00:02:27,990
I'd love to sing a song here in the church!

17
00:02:32,740 --> 00:02:35,530
That's an odd, heart-warming 
thing to bring up at random.

18
00:02:35,530 --> 00:02:39,330
We were in the middle of discussing the very 
important business of protecting His Holiness...

19
00:02:39,330 --> 00:02:41,000
It'll be okay!

20
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:43,750
There won't be an attack 
or an assassination.

21
00:02:43,750 --> 00:02:47,340
And since I can't do anything 
to help with guarding people...

22
00:02:48,880 --> 00:02:50,380
True.

23
00:02:52,590 --> 00:02:56,140
It might be safest for Lloyd 
to be in the Daen Cathedral.

24
00:02:57,640 --> 00:03:00,390
I'd love to sing with you!

25
00:03:00,390 --> 00:03:02,350
But that calls for rehearsal.

26
00:03:02,810 --> 00:03:04,980
I'll help as well.

27
00:03:06,900 --> 00:03:10,530
So, what were you trying to 
pull with that nonsense, boss?

28
00:03:11,320 --> 00:03:12,660
Well...

29
00:03:12,660 --> 00:03:17,670
I think that the pope himself 
might be the mastermind.

30
00:03:17,670 --> 00:03:20,550
What are you basing that on?!

31
00:03:20,550 --> 00:03:23,430
The most fundamental of 
deductions, my dear Jihriel.

32
00:03:23,430 --> 00:03:26,340
He probably has a ton of 
spare time on his hands!

33
00:03:26,340 --> 00:03:30,180
And you need a ton of time and 
money to build a shop like that!

34
00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:30,430
I'm bored!

35
00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:32,940
Let's make
chimeras!

36
00:03:30,510 --> 00:03:32,930
<i>That really is pretty elementary!</i>

37
00:03:32,930 --> 00:03:34,390
Which is why,

38
00:03:34,390 --> 00:03:37,940
during the Great Advent Festival, 
I'll be waiting here for the trouble to start.

39
00:03:37,940 --> 00:03:41,190
You guys should probably 
rest up while you can.

40
00:03:44,530 --> 00:03:45,900
Practice!

41
00:03:50,790 --> 00:03:55,710
Episode 20: Invasion

42
00:03:51,710 --> 00:04:01,470
Rumble Rumble Rumble

43
00:03:53,790 --> 00:03:58,170
Yeah. Prince Lloyd will do something 
about whoever's behind all this.

44
00:03:58,670 --> 00:04:00,500
We have to protect the city!

45
00:04:09,640 --> 00:04:14,270
And how, exactly, are you a mere prince?

46
00:04:22,480 --> 00:04:24,990
He was able to cut through 
Prince Lloyd's Luxa!

47
00:04:24,990 --> 00:04:27,990
I'm more impressed by how he seems 
fine after that ass kicking!

48
00:04:30,660 --> 00:04:32,030
Come on, Jihriel!

49
00:04:32,030 --> 00:04:35,790
The sooner we get rid of the chimeras, 
the sooner we can back up Prince Lloyd!

50
00:04:36,960 --> 00:04:38,080
But...

51
00:04:39,330 --> 00:04:43,750
He's so fiercely strong. 
Could Prince Lloyd really need our help?

52
00:04:43,750 --> 00:04:46,050
It stands to reason he'd be fierce.

53
00:04:46,420 --> 00:04:49,050
He's been pissed off all this time...

54
00:04:49,050 --> 00:04:52,470
over what happened before... 
and most recently.

55
00:04:52,930 --> 00:04:56,730
People represent the potential 
of magic to Prince Lloyd,

56
00:04:56,730 --> 00:04:59,600
and after seeing what's been 
done right under his nose...

57
00:04:59,600 --> 00:05:01,190
he's gonna be furious.

58
00:05:01,190 --> 00:05:03,230
That sounds like less reason to worry—

59
00:05:03,230 --> 00:05:04,520
It's the other way around!

60
00:05:04,940 --> 00:05:08,530
This pope, Guitane, 
represents that potential too!

61
00:05:08,950 --> 00:05:12,200
Look, we need to kill the 
chimeras and get back, fast!

62
00:05:15,200 --> 00:05:18,250
That attack has made something clear to me.

63
00:05:18,250 --> 00:05:23,840
I no longer care about Charles or Jihriel.

64
00:05:24,340 --> 00:05:25,460
God.

65
00:05:26,960 --> 00:05:33,220
You are a god, and by killing you, 
I will fully descend into my abyss.

66
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:37,220
If that's what you wanna believe, sure. 
You're wrong, though.

67
00:05:41,020 --> 00:05:41,980
Bring it.

68
00:05:47,690 --> 00:05:49,320
<i>Those are Crow's crows.</i>

69
00:05:49,860 --> 00:05:51,360
<i>And the signal...?</i>

70
00:05:57,580 --> 00:05:59,080
<i>Three caws...</i>

71
00:05:59,700 --> 00:06:03,960
<i>The pope's the mastermind! 
This is awful! But...</i>

72
00:06:04,330 --> 00:06:06,090
<i>it's as Lloyd predicted.</i>

73
00:06:06,750 --> 00:06:08,510
Take shelter inside of the cathedral!

74
00:06:09,710 --> 00:06:13,970
<i>That doesn't confirm that the other 
bishops are all innocent, though.</i>

75
00:06:13,970 --> 00:06:15,970
<i>Some of them might be working in tandem.</i>

76
00:06:16,390 --> 00:06:18,470
<i>Archbishop Dante...</i>

77
00:06:18,930 --> 00:06:20,520
<i>Those stitches...</i>

78
00:06:21,680 --> 00:06:22,890
<i>are suspicious</i>

79
00:06:22,890 --> 00:06:24,730
<i>because they remind me of the chimeras!</i>

80
00:06:24,980 --> 00:06:25,690
Purification!

81
00:06:27,270 --> 00:06:29,110
Thank you...

82
00:06:29,110 --> 00:06:31,650
Um... you're Archbishop...?

83
00:06:34,570 --> 00:06:36,780
Miss, you're so adorable!

84
00:06:36,780 --> 00:06:38,740
I'm gonna keep you nice and safe—

85
00:06:38,740 --> 00:06:39,040
Poison Punch!!

86
00:06:38,740 --> 00:06:40,080
Poison Punch!

87
00:06:39,120 --> 00:06:39,410
Poison Punch!!

88
00:06:39,490 --> 00:06:40,540
Poison Punch!!

89
00:06:42,620 --> 00:06:45,960
Shoot! He was so creepy I 
just reacted on reflex!

90
00:06:46,960 --> 00:06:50,260
Very nice. I'm never 
washing this cheek again.

91
00:06:50,260 --> 00:06:52,260
You really should! There's poison on it!

92
00:07:03,060 --> 00:07:06,730
Wh-What is going on here?

93
00:07:06,730 --> 00:07:08,730
Bishop Anastasia?

94
00:07:09,190 --> 00:07:14,240
Good grief. I had hoped to lop off 
your head during the chaos...

95
00:07:14,240 --> 00:07:18,740
Isn't it unbecoming of a bishop to 
carry those kind of things around?

96
00:07:18,780 --> 00:07:24,250
The Pope's Forces
Lunar Priestess Anastasia

97
00:07:19,030 --> 00:07:21,870
It is. Which is why I'll be 
tendering my resignation.

98
00:07:21,870 --> 00:07:23,910
<i>I was right, then.</i>

99
00:07:35,380 --> 00:07:37,260
The one in the middle...

100
00:07:37,260 --> 00:07:40,010
He clearly has a bizarre amount of mana.

101
00:07:41,010 --> 00:07:44,020
I am Grimoire. the Forbidden Tome!

102
00:07:41,310 --> 00:07:44,020
The Pope's Forces, A-Rank Chimera

103
00:07:41,310 --> 00:07:44,020
Grimoire (?) the Forbidden Tome

104
00:07:44,350 --> 00:07:46,690
It... It can't be!

105
00:07:47,020 --> 00:07:50,230
Grimoire? As in...

106
00:07:50,230 --> 00:07:52,320
You fool! Haven't you heard of him?!

107
00:07:52,320 --> 00:07:54,030
This is the problem with kids these days!

108
00:07:54,030 --> 00:07:57,780
He's the legendary demon who wreaked 
havoc upon the Saloum Kingdom

109
00:07:57,780 --> 00:08:00,490
in days long gone by, 
before being sealed away!

110
00:08:00,490 --> 00:08:04,200
When I was a child, parents used to scold 
their children by saying that Grimoire

111
00:08:04,200 --> 00:08:06,040
would come for them if they misbehaved!

112
00:08:06,580 --> 00:08:09,540
But now the seal has been broken?!

113
00:08:09,540 --> 00:08:11,590
Grimoire will come for you...

114
00:08:11,590 --> 00:08:13,760
...if you misbehave?

115
00:08:15,050 --> 00:08:16,300
Here I am.

116
00:08:19,300 --> 00:08:23,480
I am no other! And now, in this kingdom 
that had the nerve to imprison me...

117
00:08:23,480 --> 00:08:25,730
I will have my revenge!

118
00:08:27,270 --> 00:08:28,980
<i>Why grey?!</i>

119
00:08:35,650 --> 00:08:39,990
Hey, Mumbles! I don't mind 
acting as a distraction,

120
00:08:40,280 --> 00:08:42,780
but what the hell are we 
supposed to do next?!

121
00:08:42,780 --> 00:08:46,000
I wonder if the church 
will be okay without us.

122
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:47,120
Pay attention!

123
00:08:47,710 --> 00:08:51,710
The church has that old bag, Melissa, 
to look after it. It'll be fine!

124
00:08:51,710 --> 00:08:54,750
She might not look like much, 
but she's pretty great at what she does,

125
00:08:53,500 --> 00:08:55,670
You needn't worry.

126
00:08:54,750 --> 00:08:56,210
with magic and everything.

127
00:08:56,210 --> 00:08:59,630
She's not impressive as me, 
the great Batts, though!

128
00:08:59,630 --> 00:09:01,090
Pay attention, damn it!

129
00:09:01,090 --> 00:09:03,970
<i>The messenger crows are 
behaving strangely, too.</i>

130
00:09:03,970 --> 00:09:05,890
<i>Especially the ones toward 
the center of town.</i>

131
00:09:05,890 --> 00:09:07,980
<i>There's something else going on here.</i>

132
00:09:13,360 --> 00:09:15,530
That dude can really move.

133
00:09:20,240 --> 00:09:23,570
You might be the second 
prince's goons, or whatever,

134
00:09:23,570 --> 00:09:26,120
but that don't mean I trust any of you...

135
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:31,620
The Pope's Forces, SS-Rank Chimera

136
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:31,620
Nether-Beast, Black Dragon Chimera

137
00:09:34,920 --> 00:09:37,630
Whoa. Whoa!

138
00:09:38,050 --> 00:09:39,970
What the hell is that thing?!

139
00:09:41,630 --> 00:09:44,390
Mumbles, what are we gonna—

140
00:09:47,970 --> 00:09:49,520
<i>Is he serious?</i>

141
00:09:50,850 --> 00:09:56,150
<i>He's going up against that monster? 
Without even hesitating?</i>

142
00:09:57,110 --> 00:10:00,650
Batts, men shouldn't run 
their mouths so much.

143
00:10:00,650 --> 00:10:03,320
It's all about communicating with your back.

144
00:10:03,910 --> 00:10:06,830
I get you now, Dante.

145
00:10:07,200 --> 00:10:12,920
Just now I could hear that quiet bastard's 
kick-ass, rocking shout!

146
00:10:14,540 --> 00:10:19,170
Looks like I'm taking another step 
towards becoming a great bishop!

147
00:10:29,520 --> 00:10:32,020
Aomaki

148
00:10:29,520 --> 00:10:32,020
Akamaki

149
00:10:32,750 --> 00:10:37,830
<i>In that instant, time was scattered like 
the petals of a flower in the wind,</i>

150
00:10:37,830 --> 00:10:39,540
<i>moving every so slowly...</i>

151
00:10:40,380 --> 00:10:46,030
<i>giving the foe who defies me a chance 
to reflect on their entire life.</i>

152
00:10:46,510 --> 00:10:49,540
<i>A vision playing out at 
five centimeters per second...</i>

153
00:10:49,540 --> 00:10:51,760
<i>But realistically...</i>

154
00:10:54,200 --> 00:10:57,920
<i>a vertical drop at the speed of sound 
where you can't break your fall!</i>

155
00:10:57,920 --> 00:10:59,420
<i></i><i>Akamaki</i><i></i>

156
00:10:57,920 --> 00:10:59,420
<i></i><i>Aomaki</i><i></i>

157
00:11:01,170 --> 00:11:02,920
Did that sate you?

158
00:11:04,920 --> 00:11:09,430
Your fleeting life, so much like 
falling cherry blossoms...

159
00:11:11,140 --> 00:11:14,930
because my Rakkaken is a one-hit kill!

160
00:11:14,600 --> 00:11:16,480
The Pope's Forces, A-Rank Chimera

161
00:11:14,600 --> 00:11:16,480
Shakra, Falling Flowers Fist

162
00:11:18,390 --> 00:11:21,230
<i>Wh-What just happened?!</i>

163
00:11:22,520 --> 00:11:24,910
<i>Even through the eyes of 
a martial arts layman...</i>

164
00:11:24,910 --> 00:11:27,990
Bunhead's offense was truly incredible.

165
00:11:28,360 --> 00:11:32,950
As impossible as it seemed, she was 
able to restrain those six arms,

166
00:11:32,950 --> 00:11:34,910
and it looked like they melded together...

167
00:11:35,580 --> 00:11:38,920
Before Bunhead was slammed into the ground!

168
00:11:38,920 --> 00:11:40,330
Bunhead!

169
00:11:40,330 --> 00:11:42,170
Hey! Are you okay over there?!

170
00:11:42,170 --> 00:11:43,540
It's pointless.

171
00:11:43,540 --> 00:11:48,180
As I told you, my Rakkaken 
kills with a single blow.

172
00:11:48,180 --> 00:11:52,680
Are you worms trying to 
make me repeat myself?

173
00:11:53,140 --> 00:11:56,470
Why do the two of you have 
the same face, anyway?

174
00:11:54,310 --> 00:11:56,690
It's because we're, well, twins...

175
00:11:54,310 --> 00:11:56,690
Gulp

176
00:11:56,470 --> 00:11:57,930
That's making this twice as tiresome.

177
00:11:58,520 --> 00:12:00,690
So irritating...

178
00:12:00,690 --> 00:12:02,690
I'll kill you both at once!

179
00:12:12,080 --> 00:12:13,920
Bunhead!

180
00:12:13,920 --> 00:12:16,340
Impossible! You should be dead!

181
00:12:16,340 --> 00:12:19,210
Without being able to break your fall, 
your brain should be all over—

182
00:12:20,340 --> 00:12:22,430
I did break my fall, though.

183
00:12:23,390 --> 00:12:24,850
At the last second.

184
00:12:25,140 --> 00:12:28,060
I happened to stumble upon 
a delicate-looking arm...

185
00:12:29,060 --> 00:12:32,100
So I ripped it off, 
and made a cushion out of it.

186
00:12:34,440 --> 00:12:38,610
You'd have been better off 
watching your life flash before you.

187
00:12:38,860 --> 00:12:42,110
Y'know, my life really 
did flash before my eyes.

188
00:12:42,400 --> 00:12:44,280
And it reminded me of something...

189
00:12:46,200 --> 00:12:48,120
The Rakkaken—the Falling Flower Fist—

190
00:12:48,120 --> 00:12:50,870
A phantom style of martial arts that 
vanished in a single generation,

191
00:12:50,870 --> 00:12:52,580
with no other disciples...

192
00:12:52,580 --> 00:12:57,710
I guess the wraith of Shakra, the founder of
the Rakkaken form, is inside that chimera.

193
00:12:59,250 --> 00:13:03,260
My Rakkaken was perfected 
after I gained this chimera body!

194
00:13:03,550 --> 00:13:07,260
Superhuman reflexes afforded by six 
eyes that no human could have!

195
00:13:07,260 --> 00:13:10,020
Grappling techniques made 
possible with six arms!

196
00:13:10,020 --> 00:13:12,520
Instant throws that don't allow 
for breaking of the fall!

197
00:13:12,520 --> 00:13:14,480
And you dare to—

198
00:13:14,480 --> 00:13:16,940
Why exactly do you want to be strong?

199
00:13:18,270 --> 00:13:19,610
Bunhead...

200
00:13:19,610 --> 00:13:21,070
Bunhead...

201
00:13:22,110 --> 00:13:23,780
Millions of times...

202
00:13:24,030 --> 00:13:28,240
I punched, and punched, and trained 
myself to the point of tears.

203
00:13:28,240 --> 00:13:30,780
And why did I do it? For the sake of others?

204
00:13:31,450 --> 00:13:33,160
I did it to be popular.

205
00:13:34,210 --> 00:13:35,620
Madness.

206
00:13:36,250 --> 00:13:40,840
You dare stick your neck into 
this sacred battle for such a—

207
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:41,670
What about you?

208
00:13:42,050 --> 00:13:46,840
Look what it's done to your face... 
Are you telling me it was for no reason?

209
00:13:52,810 --> 00:13:57,520
There is no way I'll lose to you, 
not after you've cast aside your humanity!

210
00:13:58,520 --> 00:14:02,940
<i>Her beliefs... 
Her qi techniques... Her stance...</i>

211
00:14:02,940 --> 00:14:04,320
I knew it...

212
00:14:04,700 --> 00:14:06,280
<i>The Hundred Flowers Fist!</i>

213
00:14:06,740 --> 00:14:10,580
<i>I don't know if I should 
thank or curse the gods.</i>

214
00:14:10,580 --> 00:14:13,540
<i>To run across you again...</i>

215
00:14:13,870 --> 00:14:16,830
Warrior

216
00:14:16,830 --> 00:14:18,830
Shakra...

217
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:25,050
If you fail a hundred times, 
then simply try a million times more.

218
00:14:25,880 --> 00:14:27,760
<i>It's illogical.</i>

219
00:14:30,050 --> 00:14:32,680
Don't let a single loss discourage you.

220
00:14:33,720 --> 00:14:36,740
<i>I am too logical for that!</i>

221
00:14:36,740 --> 00:14:38,560
<i>I chose to be chimera instead of a human!</i>

222
00:14:38,560 --> 00:14:42,690
<i>To have an unaging, superhuman body! 
That is clearly the logical choice!</i>

223
00:14:42,690 --> 00:14:45,320
<i>And she says I've thrown something away?</i>

224
00:14:45,320 --> 00:14:50,200
<i>A little girl who's been barely 
alive for a few years? Unacceptable.</i>

225
00:14:50,200 --> 00:14:53,790
<i>Imbecile. Is she gonna charge 
straight at me again?</i>

226
00:14:53,790 --> 00:14:55,200
<i>The sheer stupidity...</i>

227
00:14:55,200 --> 00:14:57,080
<i>I will strike her down.</i>

228
00:15:00,790 --> 00:15:02,210
<i>Idiot.</i>

229
00:15:05,460 --> 00:15:07,630
<i>I will end you.</i>

230
00:15:31,820 --> 00:15:33,490
<i>It felt like revenge,</i>

231
00:15:33,490 --> 00:15:36,830
<i>as my field of vision was obscured as if 
a flower petal blown right across my eyes,</i>

232
00:15:36,830 --> 00:15:38,330
<i>ever so fluidly...</i>

233
00:15:38,790 --> 00:15:41,750
Rakkaken

234
00:15:41,750 --> 00:15:44,380
Please! You must inherit my techniques!

235
00:15:47,010 --> 00:15:49,260
If you don't, the Rakkaken will die out!

236
00:15:52,010 --> 00:15:54,510
Didn't you lose to Hyakkaken?

237
00:15:59,020 --> 00:16:01,520
Give up your school, old man.

238
00:16:02,810 --> 00:16:04,770
<i>It's over.</i>

239
00:16:05,230 --> 00:16:09,030
<i>To hell with your hundred efforts... 
your million efforts!</i>

240
00:16:09,400 --> 00:16:12,700
<i>One loss was enough to 
bring it all to an end!</i>

241
00:16:13,740 --> 00:16:15,370
<i>I curse you.</i>

242
00:16:20,410 --> 00:16:25,040
<i>It hurts. I'm so angry. And desperate.</i>

243
00:16:25,040 --> 00:16:29,170
<i>Desperate for the power 
to kill in an instant...</i>

244
00:16:34,430 --> 00:16:39,560
Come along with me. I'll prepare 
a wonderful body for you.

245
00:16:39,850 --> 00:16:41,440
To what end?

246
00:16:41,440 --> 00:16:43,310
For the sake of others?

247
00:16:43,940 --> 00:16:45,610
I did it to be popular.

248
00:16:48,070 --> 00:16:52,280
<i>The impact of the blow was so powerful</i>

249
00:16:52,280 --> 00:16:55,370
<i>it forced my consciousness 
back into the present.</i>

250
00:17:02,080 --> 00:17:05,080
<i>A hundred flowering fists, 
flying as fiercely as the winds of a storm.</i>

251
00:17:05,790 --> 00:17:10,590
<i>But... Rakkaken will not fall!
Will not be defeated!</i>

252
00:17:07,630 --> 00:17:10,800
Rakkaken

253
00:17:29,360 --> 00:17:32,320
Great work, Bunhead!

254
00:17:32,320 --> 00:17:36,870
You see that, you monster?! Now that 
it's over, you didn't amount to...

255
00:17:38,580 --> 00:17:39,830
<i>No.</i>

256
00:17:41,120 --> 00:17:44,370
<i>It obviously wasn't an easy victory!</i>

257
00:17:44,660 --> 00:17:47,130
<i>Tearing limbs off, 
every time she was grabbed...</i>

258
00:17:47,130 --> 00:17:49,380
<i>Over and over again!</i>

259
00:17:50,550 --> 00:17:52,380
<i>Every time!</i>

260
00:17:53,630 --> 00:17:56,930
<i>She literally tore victory 
from the hands of defeat!</i>

261
00:17:58,090 --> 00:18:03,140
<i>Against a monster that was a haphazard 
mish-mash of stolen strengths...</i>

262
00:18:03,140 --> 00:18:05,690
<i>Her diligence won the day!</i>

263
00:18:05,690 --> 00:18:09,770
<i>This was a victory... for the human body!</i>

264
00:18:10,610 --> 00:18:13,440
How's... that...?

265
00:18:13,900 --> 00:18:16,320
Do you see...?

266
00:18:17,410 --> 00:18:20,660
The strength of... my Rakkaken...

267
00:18:20,660 --> 00:18:22,660
She's still alive?!

268
00:18:22,660 --> 00:18:24,830
Let's purify her to end it.

269
00:18:24,830 --> 00:18:27,790
Yeah. I saw it.

270
00:18:29,290 --> 00:18:32,670
Pretty impressive! 
You're still trying to throw me.

271
00:18:35,130 --> 00:18:39,340
You win. Those were some amazing grapples.

272
00:18:40,180 --> 00:18:43,220
And you never gave up.

273
00:18:43,890 --> 00:18:47,310
It was very human... and very handsome!

274
00:18:51,020 --> 00:18:53,020
I see...

275
00:18:53,020 --> 00:18:54,730
<i>I see, now.</i>

276
00:18:57,400 --> 00:19:04,080
<i>All I really longed for... was someone 
to recognize what I'd accomplished.</i>

277
00:19:18,630 --> 00:19:20,430
Pyrlanse Incinis!

278
00:19:21,590 --> 00:19:24,010
Wahh!

279
00:19:25,060 --> 00:19:29,810
Galilea! My power isn't 
working on them at all!

280
00:19:29,810 --> 00:19:31,060
Makes sense!

281
00:19:31,060 --> 00:19:34,860
They're basically meat puppets, 
and probably aren't too sensitive to pain!

282
00:19:35,150 --> 00:19:37,070
Plus, the goathead is one of those

283
00:19:37,070 --> 00:19:40,660
pains in the ass that 
regenerates itself with mana!

284
00:19:41,160 --> 00:19:45,330
Its sorcery is potent, as well! 
How can we fight it?!

285
00:19:45,790 --> 00:19:48,910
You two bishops, keep the church safe.

286
00:19:48,910 --> 00:19:51,880
Talia, back me up with divine sorcery!

287
00:19:51,880 --> 00:19:54,090
I'll look for an opening and then 
restrain them with my webs!

288
00:19:57,880 --> 00:19:59,840
Restrain me?

289
00:19:59,840 --> 00:20:05,260
You think that's really going to work 
against I, Grimoire the Forbidden Tome?!

290
00:20:06,600 --> 00:20:09,600
Oh, knock it off! We know you're a phony!

291
00:20:09,600 --> 00:20:11,600
Hang on, Talia.

292
00:20:11,600 --> 00:20:12,810
What is it?

293
00:20:12,810 --> 00:20:15,650
Is it possible our guy is the phony?

294
00:20:15,650 --> 00:20:19,820
What are you saying, Galilea?! 
Grim's so much more...

295
00:20:20,650 --> 00:20:22,610
Hey!

296
00:20:20,900 --> 00:20:22,610
Hey!

297
00:20:22,610 --> 00:20:26,330
I picked up some pancakes for you guys.

298
00:20:26,330 --> 00:20:28,370
He fell asleep.

299
00:20:28,370 --> 00:20:30,120
He sure did.

300
00:20:30,120 --> 00:20:32,870
...way more... cute.

301
00:20:32,870 --> 00:20:34,380
Yeah.

302
00:20:34,380 --> 00:20:37,380
Then... is he the real deal?

303
00:20:37,710 --> 00:20:39,130
Behold!

304
00:20:39,130 --> 00:20:45,390
The power of the ancient sorcery wielded 
by Grimoire, the Forbidden Tome!

305
00:20:45,550 --> 00:20:47,640
Smash

306
00:20:57,770 --> 00:21:00,610
D... Don't tell me?

307
00:21:03,240 --> 00:21:04,660
Arctis Obscura.

308
00:21:20,170 --> 00:21:24,430
What the hell? 
Not even a demon on the inside.

309
00:21:24,930 --> 00:21:25,680
Here.

310
00:21:26,390 --> 00:21:28,470
You two purify that clown.

311
00:21:30,770 --> 00:21:35,400
Galilea, you're gonna focus on plugging 
the various holes around town.

312
00:21:35,400 --> 00:21:36,850
R-Right!

313
00:21:40,120 --> 00:21:42,970
So, who were you, anyway?

314
00:21:42,970 --> 00:21:48,060
Well, I was actually a sorcerer who studied 
ancient magic when I was alive...

315
00:21:43,480 --> 00:21:48,070
Heh heh heh...

316
00:21:48,060 --> 00:21:50,960
And that was how I became 
a fan of Mr. Grimoire!

317
00:21:50,590 --> 00:21:51,450
Purify.

318
00:21:55,730 --> 00:21:58,450
So, you think that was...?

319
00:21:58,950 --> 00:22:01,590
Could it be...?

320
00:23:35,520 --> 00:23:38,810
<i>My Rakkaken will live on! It will never die!</i>

321
00:23:38,810 --> 00:23:42,010
<i>It's yours now, Hyakkaken girl.</i>

322
00:23:42,010 --> 00:23:44,270
<i>Next time, on Episode 21:</i>

323
00:23:44,270 --> 00:23:45,860
<i>The Moon and Tonkatsu.</i>

324
00:23:44,270 --> 00:23:50,100
The Moon and Tonkatsu

325
00:23:44,270 --> 00:23:50,100
Episode 21

326
00:23:45,860 --> 00:23:49,370
<i>You will witness the depths of sorcery.</i>

